  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` to `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as `8c029a7`. The five new tests pass. I didn't run the wider suite or `npm run fast`.\n\n- **Behaviour:** text that fits is returned unchanged. Longer text keeps its start and end around a single `…`, and the result is never longer than `max`. When the kept characters split unevenly, the start gets the extra one. For example, `truncateMiddle('abcdefghij', 6)` returns `abc…ij`.\n- **Edge cases:** `max` of 1 returns just `…`, and `max` of 0 or less returns an empty string.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/truncate.test.ts` uses `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`. I also added a weight for it in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **Commit title:** the repo convention is to end the title with the task id in parentheses, but I wasn't given one and didn't invent one. The title has no id. If you give me the id I can amend the commit.",
